  "details": "The microphone button has different tooltips depending on the mode and the state of the microphone. However, the tooltips use inconsistent terms to refer to the microphone, such as:\n\n- **Microphone** in Always On/Off mode.\n\n- **Audio input device** in Toggle mode.\n\n- **To talk** in Push-to-talk mode.\n\nMoreover, the tooltips in Always On/Off mode are not working properly. They seem to display the **key name** instead of the actual text message, resulting in an extra ‘Tooltip/’ prefix and no translation applied.\n\nI suggest **fixing** the tooltips in Always On/Off mode and using a **single term for all the tooltips**.\n\nI recommend using the term **microphone**, as it is consistent with the rest of the UI, except for the device selection menu.\n\nWe can keep **Audio input device** as tech detail in device selection menu.",
